FujiNet Go PMD 85 desktop -- rolling notes
==========================================

Done (2026-11-16, first pass)
-----------------------------
- Repo skeleton after fujinet-go-adam-desktop/PORTING.md, derived from
  fujinet-go-coco-desktop (same transport direction: FujiNet listens).
- cmake/Dependencies.cmake: GPMD85Emulator (mborik main 10c6ad7) and
  fujinet-firmware (same pin as the CoCo app, COCO target) cloned at their
  pins; GPMD85_SRC / FUJINET_SRC overrides.
- cmake/StageGPMD85.cmake: stages only the machine sources (CPU, memory,
  chips, interfaces, PMD 32, MIF 85, ROM/MegaModule, SAASound, CommonUtils)
  into core/gpmd85-generated. Upstream's app layer (TEmulator, ScreenPMD85,
  SoundDriver, Settings, gui/) is never built. No upstream file is edited:
  tools/gpmd85/support/shim/SDL.h stands in for SDL on their include path.
- core/pmd85/pmd85_host.cpp: the headless machine (model build, frame loop,
  frame render, mixer, joystick GPIO, key queue, live colour change,
  reconfigure); pmd85_becker.cpp: Becker port (DriveWire/TCP 3Eh/3Fh) from
  the GPMD85Emulator becker-port WIP: lazy reconnect, non-blocking, a bounded
  reply wait so DriveWire transactions finish within a frame, and the
  ROM-module download into the MegaModule.
- Session (pmd85session.h): FujiNet first + listener wait, 50 Hz wall-clock
  pacing, frame store, settings, paths, embedded firmware (GPMD85Emulator
  rom/ + the FujiNet CONFIG loader module), media import, FujiNet port
  conflict warning, PMD85_BECKER_PORT override (rewrites the runtime tree's
  [BOIP] port to match).
- FujiNet runtime: tools/fujinet/build-fujinet-desktop.sh (COCO target,
  [BOIP] port=65505, devicename=PMD 85, web UI 127.0.0.1:64003).
- Tests: input_map, hostport, boot_smoke (all 8 models), becker (fake
  DriveWire server incl. a 2-page ROM download), session (real time),
  drivewire_smoke (the real FujiNet, end to end).
- GNOME frontend (GTK4/libadwaita, built in the GNOME 51 SDK): display (4:3
  TV default, square, integer), menus (model, ROM module, colours, RESET,
  cold restart, fullscreen, import, FujiNet config/log), preferences, LEDs,
  link/MegaModule status, embedded FujiNet web UI.
- tools/dev-gnome.sh: sdl/build/run/shell in the GNOME 51 SDK, always with
  the home mount (without it settings and the FujiNet tree are lost).
- Display: "Sharp" scaling (default; Nearest/Smooth kept), picture snapped
  to device pixels, integer mode in device pixels.
- Debugger engine (core/debugger, pmd85debug.h): pause/step/over/out/run
  to/frames, exec/read/write/IN/OUT breakpoints with conditions, registers
  and memory edits, memory map (ROM vs RAM via a derived probe), trace, I/O
  log, port names, chips view, symbols (EQU / z88dk .map), prompt, DriveWire
  trace incl. the ROM-module download. 8080 disassembler (Intel or Z80
  spelling), checked against GPMD85's tables. No upstream patch: accesses
  are decoded from the instruction in the host's per-instruction hook.
- The FujiNet module is attached on every model with a module slot; the 2
  and 2A auto-run it, elsewhere it is started from the monitor.
- ROM module "Module file": the user's own .rmm (32 KB ROM pack) or .mrm
  (MegaModule) image (setting module_file); menu and Preferences chooser.
- Tape deck: GPMD85's TapeBrowser staged unchanged (the shim's Emulator.h
  gives it its four settings); flash load and the Mato save trap ported
  from TEmulator::CpuTimerCallback (the body is flashed, the header plays in
  real time, as upstream). Tape menu: Load, Save As, Play, Stop, Rewind,
  Eject (asks when recordings are unsaved); status in the subtitle; the tape
  is remembered (tape_file). Preferences: Flash load (on), Tape sound (off).
- FujiNet's own restart (web UI Restart: exit(75) in fujinet-pc) ends the
  in-process runtime instead; a watchdog restarts it (as the Atari 800 app;
  3 restarts in 30 s and it stays stopped). /restart?exit=1 stops it.
- FujiNet Web UI opens in the system browser (as the Atari 800 app; no
  WebKitGTK); the Console Log window belongs to the app (grouped, our icon).
- FujiNet menu as in the Atari 800 app: FujiNet Web UI, Console Log,
  Restart FujiNet (FujiNet alone, the PMD keeps running), Import to SD
  Card... (several at once), Open SD Folder.

Next
----
- Module start hints (pmd85session_module_hint, toasted on a model change):
  the 85-1 (JOB 000001100000) and 85-3 (JUMP FFF0, or the 85-2
  compatibility switch, which auto-runs it) are confirmed, the 85-2 and 2A
  boot it by themselves; the Alfas get a generic line -- find their command.
- Debugger window, after use: a Video tab (VRAM, the attribute bits, the
  colour profile); a help page; per-tab polish found while using it.
- Debugger symbols: the 85-1 and 85-2 monitors have tables (2A uses the
  85-2's); the 85-3 (E000h), Mato, Alfa and Consul monitors have none --
  add when a commented listing turns up (tools/gpmd85/extract-monitor-
  symbols.py takes the listings; regenerate with it).
- (done) GNOME debugger window: F12 / menu, from the CoCo app's window:
  Console, Disassembly, Memory, Breakpoints (incl. IN/OUT), Watches, I/O
  (map, chips, I/O log), Trace, History, Symbols, FujiNet; Intel/Z80 and
  hex-style selectors. PMD85_OPEN_DEBUGGER=1 opens it at start.
- (done) Tape browser (Machine > Tape > Tape Browser, Alt+T): the
  tape's blocks with the position and STOP marker; double-click moves the
  position; context menu: marker, move up/down, delete; Append Tape; auto
  stop (next file / marker / end); hex/dec. Previous/Next File (menu and
  browser) step over data blocks to the next header.
- (done) FujiNet restart in-process, from the Atari app's v0.6.1: between
  runs the images are unmounted, the hosts reset and the bus's shutdown
  flag lowered (it made every TNFS request of the next run "succeed" with
  garbage); TNFS gives up at once while shutting down; a runtime that does
  not stop is not restarted on top of; the log pipe is close-on-exec. Ours
  too: the DriveWire bus closes its BoIP listener at shutdown (it stayed
  open into the next run). fujinet_restart_test lists SD and a local tnfsd
  ($PMD85_TNFSD) across restarts. The console log window appends (a cursor
  reader, fujinet_desktop_read_log) and keeps the reader's place.
- Upstream (fujinet-firmware): the DriveWire bus's shutdown() leaving the
  BoIP listener open, and setup() not lowering shuttingDown, affect any
  in-process restart; worth a PR with the Atari app's SIO equivalents. Also
  its shutdown() not shutting the devices down (a TODO there): the Fuji
  device's hostMounted[] outlived the run, so MOUNT HOST of a host CONFIG
  had browsed answered "mounted" without mounting (error 144 on OPEN
  DIRECTORY). The wrapper calls fujiDevice::shutdown() for now.
- (done) Hotkeys on Alt, as upstream (Ctrl is STOP, Shift the PMD's): Alt+F
  fullscreen, Alt+C colors (cycles), Alt+T tape browser, Alt+P tape
  play/stop, Alt+F5 RESET, Alt+Shift+F5 cold restart.
- (done) Colors: Black & White (the TV), Green (the same, green monitor),
  RGBM, ColorACE; Monochrome dropped ("colors" setting; the old
  "color_profile" carries over).
- Tape, later: a "Play" that also types the load command (MGLD nn on the
  monitor, LOAD in BASIC -- needs to know which is running).
- (done) Gamepads -> the 4004/482 joysticks (1 on GPIO A, 2 on GPIO B; A is
  the PMD 32's when it is connected): SDL3 hot-plug thread after the Atari
  app's v0.7.0 design -- sources merged per joystick (opposite directions
  cancel), pads take the free joysticks in order or one set by hand and
  remembered ("pad_assign"); D-pad and left stick ("analog_stick") steer,
  South/East/shoulders/triggers fire; raw HID joysticks by hat 0, axes 0/1,
  buttons 0-3. Preferences > Input lists the pads; connect toasts.
  gamepad_test drives it with SDL virtual pads; joystick_test reads the
  ports with a PMD program.
- (done) Mouse 602 (GPMD85Emulator's, port 8Ch; PIT timer 1 clocks it,
  timer 0 interrupts): Machine > Peripherals switch (85-1..3, Consul 2717);
  the host pointer over the picture moves it by PMD pixels, its buttons are
  the mouse's (middle = both, as upstream); leaving the screen and coming
  back is no move; the host pointer hidden over the picture (Input page).
  mouse_test reads port 8Ch with a PMD program.
- (done) PMD 32 disk drive (GPMD85Emulator's Pmd32, drives A-D on GPIO):
  Machine > PMD 32 Disks (a submenu per drive: Insert Disk..., Eject, Write
  Protected; "Connect / Disconnect the PMD 32" under a Connected / Not connected title), changed in the running
  drive without a restart; images and protection in settings (pmd32_a..d,
  pmd32_wp_a..d), kept across model changes; a floppy light by the LEDs.
  An 85-3 boots MIKROS (CP/M) from drive A. pmd32_test.
- PMD 32, later: the SD-card extensions (sdRoot, images.cfg geometries,
  extraCommands) in Preferences; a new blank disk; drag and drop.
- Import to SD Card takes ROM modules only (.rmm .mrm): FujiNet serves a
  PMD nothing else.
- Gamepads, later: remappable buttons (a pad button -> a PMD key, as the
  Atari app's Input page), keys as a joystick (upstream's JT_KEYS), the
  drawn Controllers window. The flatpak manifest needs --device=all (or
  input) for /dev/input, as tools/dev-gnome.sh run now has.
- Keyboard options apply by cold restart; make exchZY/numpad live.
- (done) F12 is K11 on every platform; the debugger is on Alt+F12 (GNOME;
  KDE and Windows to follow), the macOS one will be Option+F12 in the main
  window plus View > Debugger on Cmd+D (the Atari app's way): done.
- macOS function keys: F11 (K10, which FujiNet CONFIG boots with) is
  often Mission Control's "Show Desktop", and F11/F12 are media keys
  unless Fn is held or "Use F1, F2, etc. keys as standard function keys"
  is on. Say so in the app (the Settings keyboard note has F11 already)
  and in the README.
- macOS (AppKit) frontend (frontends/macos, from the CoCo app's): the Metal
  display (with the Sharp scaling in its shader), keyboard (modifiers as
  the PMD's keys via flagsChanged; the app's keys are Command ones), Mouse
  602, the menu bar (Model, ROM Module, PMD 32 Disks, Tape, Colors,
  FujiNet), Settings, the Tape window, the console log. Built only on CI
  (no Apple toolchain here); tried by hand on macOS 14.6 (arm64), fine.
  The debugger window (Option+F12 or View > Debugger, Cmd+D): the GNOME
  one's ten tabs in the CoCo macOS window's shape; built only on CI so far.
  Next: drag and drop of tapes/disks.
- (done) Debugger and the PMD's mirrored I/O decode: the emulator's port
  decode is one table (pmd85host_port_devs), read by the port names and the
  debugger. A port breakpoint stops at every mirror of the register it
  reaches ("exact" / the Exact checkbox: that number only); the I/O log
  filter takes a port or range (with mirrors), =port, or a chip/register
  name, and is a capture filter (pmd85debug_io_log_set_ports: only those
  ports are recorded, so the keyboard scan does not push a rare one out);
  the I/O tab and the console's "ports" show the decode table. Port names
  show while running too. Its hint sits under the filter (no window resize
  while typing).
- (done) FujiNet CONFIG is fujinet-config.rmm (was fujinet-config-loader.rmm):
  FujiNetWIFI/fujinet-config 968d482 behind fujinet-config-loader-pmd85
  c294cd9 (logo and progress bar). A bundled ROM still exactly as an earlier
  version shipped it is updated (or, under a retired name, removed) at the
  next start; superseded_roms in core/src/paths.c lists them, a file the
  user changed is never touched. Provenance in tools/gpmd85/roms/README.md.
- (done) GNOME: a key's release lets go of what its press was (by keycode).
  With Shift held Alt_L is Meta_L, so Shift+Alt+F5 could leave Alt or Meta
  held in the machine, and GPMD85 blanks the PMD keyboard while either is.
- (done) The session test waits for machine time (frames), not wall time:
  a stalled CI host drops frames.
- Then KDE and Windows.
- CI: linux.yml (Arch container: GTK 4.16) and macos.yml (hosted macos-15,
  arm64; static SDL3 and OpenSSL, ad-hoc signed .app zip as an artifact).
  Later: windows, flatpak, a universal macOS build, release.
- Flatpak manifests, metainfo, screenshots, README.
- Upstream: tell the family's display-widget author (Thomas Cherryhomes,
  fujinet-go-coco/adam/apple2/atari800-desktop share frontends/gnome/
  display.c) about the sharp filter here: integer CPU prescale + linear
  remainder, rect snapped to device pixels (fractional scaling incl.).
  Verified on COSMIC at 130%.
- Upstream (fujinet-go-coco-desktop): its embedded WebKit web UI lacks the
  apple2/adam fix of 2026-07-28 ("create" -> system browser), so the Google
  Drive / OneDrive Authorize buttons do nothing there; the Atari 800 app and
  this one open the web UI in the browser instead. Its log/web windows also
  skip gtk_window_set_application (not grouped with the main window).
- Upstream: offer GPMD85Emulator an SDL-free machine build option, so the
  shim becomes unnecessary.
- The firmware pin has no BUILD_COCO default fnconfig.ini, so the generic
  (Atari-flavoured) host list ships -- same as the CoCo app. Consider a PMD
  default host list (and fix the same lookup in the CoCo app's script).
